 progress completes and further conversions are stopped.","cite":"9.5.3.6 STOP: Stop Conversions","anchor":13.440710850000235,"region":0,"p0":5.000014899999993,"notes":[],"checks":[{"rule":"tCSH","status":"pass","t":13.440710850000235,"detail":"CS high for 10.15 \u00b5s (needs \u2265 0.98 \u00b5s)","count":1},{"rule":"tSCCS","status":"fail","t":13.440715600000228,"detail":"1.72 \u00b5s from the last SCLK falling edge to CS high (needs \u2265 1.95 \u00b5s)","count":1}]},{"id":"last","title":"Last result","text":"DRDY falls one more time. Nobody reads it, and no new result follows.","quote":"When the STOP command is sent, the conversion in progress completes and further conversions are stopped.","cite":"9.5.3.6 STOP: Stop Conversions","anchor":13.440715750000228,"region":0,"p0":5.000019799999986,"notes":[[13.442670394530449,"Last conversion done; conversions stopped"]],"checks":[]},{"id":"standby","title":"STANDBY (04h)","text":"Low-power standby: everything off except the reference.","quote":"The STANDBY command enters low-power standby mode. All parts of the circuit are shut down except for the reference section.","cite":"9.5.3.3 STANDBY: Enter STANDBY Mode","anchor":13.446715750000228,"region":0,"p0":5.0060197999999865,"notes":[[13.446718775000223,"Bias drive off: the body floats again"],[13.446718775000223,"Standby: all circuits off except the reference"]],"checks":[{"rule":"tCSH","status":"pass","t":13.446715750000228,"detail":"CS high for 6.0 ms (needs \u2265 0.98 \u00b5s)","count":1},{"rule":"tSCCS","status":"fail","t":13.446720500000222,"detail":"1.72 \u00b5s from the last SCLK falling edge to CS high (needs \u2265 1.95 \u00b5s)","count":1}]},{"id":"bias-off","title":"Bias drive off","text":"BIASOUT stops driving, the body floats, and mains hum comes back on the electrodes. VREFP holds.","quote":"All parts of the circuit are shut down except for the reference section.","cite":"9.5.3.3 STANDBY: Enter STANDBY Mode","anchor":13.446720650000222,"region":0,"p0":5.00602469999998,"notes":[],"checks":[]},{"id":"pwdn","title":"PWDN low","text":"Full power-down. VREFP and VCAP1 discharge through the chip's resistor network.","quote":"When PWDN is pulled low, all on-chip circuitry is powered down.","cite":"9.4.3 Power-Down (PWDN)","anchor":13.506720650000222,"region":0,"p0":5.06602469999998,"notes":[[13.506720650000222,"Chip powered down: all circuits off; VCAP1 and VREFP discharge"]],"checks":[]},{"id":"supplies-off","title":"Supplies off","text":"AVDD and DVDD fall. The ESP32 loses power too, so every line goes low.","quote":"Before device power up, all digital and analog inputs must be low.","cite":"11.1 Power-Up Sequencing","anchor":14.506720800000222,"region":0,"p0":6.06602484999998,"notes":[[14.506720800000222,"Supplies off"]],"checks":[]}]}